  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kunzila Integrated Landscape Management and WASH Project (ILMWA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated Landscape Management and WASH (KILMWA) project was designed to contribute to a more prosperous and healthy population of Kunzila watershed through interventions on the ecosystem, infrastructure, community health, community organizations and financial institutions. The interventions of the project were divided into eight components of which the five components: Strengthening Community Watershed Management, livelihood enhancement and agricultural productivity increment, building local capacities, scientific monitoring, and project management were implemented through WLRC while the remaining three components that included strengthening rural WASH services, strengthening Urban WASH services and strengthening Multi-Stakeholder Coordination were implemented through SNV.

N.B. conform MINBUZA-2022.585085 top up voor - 4000003666: van  EUR 15.959.518+ top-up  EUR 4.408.137 = EUR 20.367.655 is aagepast
A one year no cost extension was approved 01-01-2025 -31-12-2025</narrative>
  </description>
